excerpt:
@brianstorms The main point to remember is that journalism is a team sport. Especially at it's highest levels, its the work product of many busy people, almost never one. 
So yeah, editors are super important because they set the quality bar for all the stories that are crushing to get published. They keep the standards, in part by asking the questions a reader might ask.
Editors enforce deadlines, and in that sense they are law. They decide what gets published, not the writers.

